# Single item, like Windows 95 — ends the session (logs you off). icewm 4.0 has NO
# --shutdown/--logout flag (only --restart/--replace), so the old `icewm --shutdown`
# was a silent no-op — the real reason "Shut Down does nothing". icewm-session
# supervises icewmbg/icewmtray/icewm; terminating them ends the session and closes
# the Xephyr window. (The ice2k shutdlg replica needs ice2k's programs/shutdown/
# tree we don't project yet; when integrated it can live in Settings > IceWM.)
prog "Shut Down..." system-shut-down sh -c "pkill -x icewm-session; pkill -x icewm"
